# NomNomytics — AI AGENT RULES
#
# This file is read by Cursor, Copilot, Windsurf, Cline, and similar tools.
# Claude Code / Codex / Gemini read AGENTS.md — the rule below is duplicated
# there verbatim and BOTH copies must stay in sync.
#
# =============================================================================
# 1. DATABASE PROTECTION RULE — HIGHEST PRIORITY, NON-NEGOTIABLE
# =============================================================================
#
# The developer's database is `database/database.sqlite`, selected by `.env`.
# Tests use `database/testing.sqlite`, selected by `.env.testing` and
# `.env.dusk.local`.
#
# NEVER run any command that could wipe, truncate, reset, or re-seed the
# development database. In particular, NEVER run these without `--env=testing`:
#
#     php artisan migrate:fresh
#     php artisan migrate:refresh
#     php artisan db:wipe
#     php artisan db:seed            (any destructive seeder)
#
# The Dusk suite TRUNCATES every table between tests. It is indiscriminate: it
# deletes rows in whichever database it is pointed at. This repository has
# ALREADY suffered data loss from exactly this — `.env` once pointed at the test
# file, so every `php artisan dusk` silently erased the developer's work.
#
# BEFORE running anything destructive, verify the target:
#
#     php artisan tinker --execute="echo config('database.connections.sqlite.database');"
#
# It MUST print `database/testing.sqlite`. If it prints `database.sqlite`, STOP.
#
# ALSO NEVER:
#   - edit `.env` to point DB_DATABASE at a test file
#   - edit `.env.testing` / `.env.dusk.local` to point at `database.sqlite`
#   - remove or weaken `assertDuskDatabaseIsDisposable()` in
#     `tests/Browser/Support/DuskDatabase.php` (it is the enforcement point)
#   - commit any `.sqlite` file
#   - "fix" a failing test by resetting the developer's data
#
# Full detail: AGENTS.md -> "Database Protection Rule".
#
# =============================================================================
# 2. TESTING
# =============================================================================
#
# The suite is DUSK-ONLY, by project policy. `tests/Unit` and `tests/Feature`
# do not exist and must not be re-added. All coverage lives in `tests/Browser/`.
#
#     php artisan dusk                      # the whole browser suite
#     php artisan dusk tests/Browser/Guest  # one directory
#
# Prerequisites that silently break the suite (each fails misleadingly):
#   - ChromeDriver must match the installed Chrome major version.
#       php artisan dusk:chrome-driver <major>
#   - `public/hot` must NOT exist, or assets load from a Vite dev server that is
#     not running: the page returns 200, renders nothing, and logs no error.
#       Remove-Item public\hot
#   - SQLite must run in WAL mode (two processes write during Dusk). The pragmas
#     live in `config/database.php`, NOT in the test bootstrap — the
#     `artisan serve` process never runs that bootstrap.
#
# =============================================================================
# 3. CONVENTIONS
# =============================================================================
#
#   - Respond in the user's language.
#   - Money is a JSON number; formatting comes from `/api/meta`. Never hard-code
#     a currency symbol.
#   - Terminology (Student / Employee / Boarder / Member) comes from the
#     institution type via `useTerminology()`. Never hard-code a noun.
#   - Multi-tenant: every tenant-owned model uses `BelongsToInstitution`. Never
#     write a query that can see across institutions without an explicit,
#     justified reason.
#   - The Software Super Admin is web-only. The mobile API blocks it in three
#     layers; do not remove any of them.
#   - React providers that render as SIBLINGS of Inertia's `<App>` must take
#     their page data as a PROP. Calling `usePage()` outside `<App>` throws and
#     blanks the entire app.